      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the given problem, we start with the equation:\n\n\\[ ab + bc + cd + da = 30 \\]\n\nand the condition:\n\n\\[ b + d = 5 \\]\n\nFirst, we can factor out common terms in the left-hand side of the equation. Notice that:\n\n\\[ ab + bc + cd + da = b(a + c) + d(a + c) \\]\n\nThis can be factored further as:\n\n\\[ b(a + c) + d(a + c) = (b + d)(a + c) \\]\n\nGiven that \\( b + d = 5 \\), we substitute this into the equation:\n\n\\[ (b + d)(a + c) = 5(a + c) \\]\n\nWe know from the problem statement that:\n\n\\[ ab + bc + cd + da = 30 \\]\n\nSo, we can substitute this into our factored equation:\n\n\\[ 5(a + c) = 30 \\]\n\nTo find \\( a + c \\), we divide both sides of the equation by 5:\n\n\\[ a + c = \\frac{30}{5} = 6 \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( a + c \\) is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{6} \\]",
